{
 "1": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"I am ~\" and \"I do ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Subject words"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Nepali",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "म",
     "ma",
     "I"
    ],
    [
     "उ",
     "u",
     "he"
    ],
    [
     "उनी",
     "unī",
     "she (polite)"
    ],
    [
     "यो",
     "yo",
     "this"
    ],
    [
     "हामी",
     "hāmī",
     "we"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2a. \"to be\" for nouns (A is B)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "\"is/am\"",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I म",
     "हुँ",
     "hũ"
    ],
    [
     "he / this उ／यो",
     "हो",
     "ho"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "म विद्यार्थी **हुँ**।",
     "ma vidyārthī **hũ**",
     "I am a student"
    ],
    [
     "उ डाक्टर **हो**।",
     "u ḍākṭar **ho**",
     "He is a doctor"
    ],
    [
     "यो किताब **हो**।",
     "yo kitāb **ho**",
     "This is a book"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2b. \"do ~\" (verb + छ)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "Ending",
    "Example (eat खानु)",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I म",
     "~**छु**",
     "खान्**छु**",
     "khān**chu**"
    ],
    [
     "he उ",
     "~**छ**",
     "खान्**छ**",
     "khān**cha**"
    ],
    [
     "she उनी",
     "~**छिन्**",
     "खान्**छिन्**",
     "khān**chin**"
    ],
    [
     "we हामी",
     "~**छौं**",
     "खान्**छौं**",
     "khān**chaũ**"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "म भात **खान्छु**।",
     "ma bhāt khānchu",
     "I eat rice"
    ],
    [
     "उ पानी **पिउँछ**।",
     "u pānī piũcha",
     "He drinks water"
    ],
    [
     "उनी स्कूल **जान्छिन्**।",
     "unī skūl jānchin",
     "She goes to school"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "3. Word order = Subject → Object → Verb"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "",
    "Subject",
    "Object",
    "Verb"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Nepali",
     "म (ma)",
     "नेपाली (nepālī)",
     "बोल्छु (bolchu)"
    ],
    [
     "English",
     "I",
     "Nepali",
     "speak"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Use **हो/हुँ** for \"A is B\" (nouns), and **verb + छ** for actions. They are different."
  }
 ],
 "2": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"I don't ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Key rule: there is no separate word for \"not\""
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The affirmative **छ (cha)** changes to the negative **दैन／दिन (daina／dina)** family — the verb itself becomes negative."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Negative conjugation (eat खानु)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "Affirmative",
    "Negative",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I म",
     "खान्छु",
     "**खाँदिनँ**",
     "khā̃**dinã**"
    ],
    [
     "he उ",
     "खान्छ",
     "**खाँदैन**",
     "khā̃**daina**"
    ],
    [
     "she उनी",
     "खान्छिन्",
     "**खाँदिनन्**",
     "khā̃**dinan**"
    ],
    [
     "we हामी",
     "खान्छौं",
     "**खाँदैनौं**",
     "khā̃**dainaũ**"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "3. Examples (affirmative → negative)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Affirmative",
    "Negative",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "म पानी पिउँछु",
     "म पानी **पिउँदिनँ** (piũdinã)",
     "I don't drink water"
    ],
    [
     "उ आउँछ",
     "उ **आउँदैन** (āũdaina)",
     "He doesn't come"
    ],
    [
     "उनी स्कूल जान्छिन्",
     "उनी स्कूल **जाँदिनन्** (jā̃dinan)",
     "She doesn't go to school"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "4. A special pattern: \"to like\""
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Part",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "मलाई",
     "malāī",
     "to me"
    ],
    [
     "मन पर्छ",
     "man parcha",
     "is liked (= like)"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "मलाई कफी मन **पर्दैनँ**।",
     "malāī kaphī man **pardainã**",
     "I don't like coffee"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "With \"like\", the subject is not \"I म\" but \"**to me मलाई**\". Literally: \"to me coffee is not liked\"."
  }
 ],
 "3": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"I did ~\". **The biggest hurdle, \"ले (le)\", appears here.**"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Past-tense endings"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "Ending",
    "Example",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I",
     "~**एँ**",
     "खा**एँ** (ate)",
     "khā**ẽ**"
    ],
    [
     "he",
     "~**यो**",
     "सुत्**यो** (slept)",
     "sut**yo**"
    ],
    [
     "she",
     "~**इन्**",
     "ग**इन्** (went)",
     "ga**in**"
    ],
    [
     "we",
     "~**यौं**",
     "हेर्**यौं** (watched)",
     "her**yaũ**"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2.【Most important】the subject of a transitive verb takes \"ले\""
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "For verbs that act on an object — eat, read, write, do — add **ले** to the subject."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "+ले",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I म",
     "**मैले**",
     "maile"
    ],
    [
     "he उसले",
     "**उसले**",
     "usle"
    ],
    [
     "she उनले",
     "**उनले**",
     "unle"
    ],
    [
     "we हामीले",
     "**हामीले**",
     "hāmīle"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "**Takes ले (transitive)**"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "**मैले** किताब पढेँ।",
     "maile kitāb paḍhẽ",
     "I read a book"
    ],
    [
     "**उसले** हिजो काम गर्यो।",
     "usle hijo kām garyo",
     "He worked yesterday"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "**No ले (intransitive: sleep, go)**"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "उ सुत्यो।",
     "u sutyo",
     "He slept"
    ],
    [
     "उनी स्कूल गइन्।",
     "unī skūl gain",
     "She went to school"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "3. How to tell them apart"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Type",
    "Examples",
    "ले"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "acts on an object (transitive)",
     "eat, read, write, do, watch",
     "**takes ले**"
    ],
    [
     "just moves (intransitive)",
     "sleep, go, come, sit",
     "no ले"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "The #1 beginner mistake is **forgetting ले**. Remember: \"action on an object = subject + ले\"."
  }
 ],
 "4": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"I didn't ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. The negative past adds \"न (na/n)\""
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Subject",
    "Past affirmative",
    "Past negative",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I",
     "खाएँ",
     "**खाइनँ**",
     "khā**inã**"
    ],
    [
     "he",
     "आयो",
     "**आएन**",
     "ā**ena**"
    ],
    [
     "she",
     "गइन्",
     "**गइनन्**",
     "ga**inan**"
    ],
    [
     "we",
     "हेर्यौं",
     "**हेरेनौँ**",
     "here**naũ**"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples (affirmative → negative)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Affirmative",
    "Negative",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "मैले खाएँ",
     "मैले **खाइनँ**",
     "I didn't eat"
    ],
    [
     "उ आयो",
     "उ **आएन**",
     "He didn't come"
    ],
    [
     "म हिजो सुतेँ",
     "म हिजो **सुतिनँ** (sutinã)",
     "I didn't sleep yesterday"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "3. \"ले\" does not disappear in the negative"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "**उसले** त्यो किताब पढेन।",
     "usle tyo kitāb paḍhena",
     "He didn't read that book"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Even in the negative, a transitive subject keeps **ले**. Don't drop it."
  }
 ],
 "5": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"I will ~\". **You can reuse the Theme 1 form.**"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Key rule: future = present form + a time word"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Time words"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Nepali",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "भोलि",
     "bholi",
     "tomorrow"
    ],
    [
     "अर्को हप्ता",
     "arko haptā",
     "next week"
    ],
    [
     "भविष्यमा",
     "bhaviṣyamā",
     "in the future"
    ],
    [
     "आज राति",
     "āja rāti",
     "tonight"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "3. How to build it = just add a time word"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Present",
    "+ time word → future",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "म स्कूल जान्छु",
     "म **भोलि** स्कूल जान्छु",
     "I'll go to school tomorrow"
    ],
    [
     "म डाक्टर बन्छु",
     "म **भविष्यमा** डाक्टर बन्छु",
     "I'll become a doctor in the future"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "उनी **अर्को हप्ता** काठमाडौं आउँछिन्।",
     "unī arko haptā kāṭhmāḍaũ āũchin",
     "She'll come to Kathmandu next week"
    ],
    [
     "उ **आज राति** साथीलाई फोन गर्छ।",
     "u āja rāti sāthīlāī phon garcha",
     "He'll call a friend tonight"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "The form is the same as Theme 1 — just place a \"when\" word near the front."
  }
 ],
 "6": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Ask \"Is it ~?\" and \"what / where / how much …?\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Yes/No questions = same word order, just rise at the end"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Statement",
    "Question",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "यो किताब हो।",
     "यो किताब **हो?**",
     "Is this a book?"
    ],
    [
     "तपाईं नेपाली **हुनुहुन्छ?**",
     "tapāī̃ nepālī hunuhuncha?",
     "Are you Nepali?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "※ **तपाईं (tapāī̃)** = polite \"you\"; **हुनुहुन्छ (hunuhuncha)** = polite \"are/do\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Question words (keep them in place)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Word",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "के",
     "ke",
     "what"
    ],
    [
     "कहाँ",
     "kahā̃",
     "where"
    ],
    [
     "कति",
     "kati",
     "how much / many"
    ],
    [
     "कहिले",
     "kahile",
     "when"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "यो **के** हो?",
     "yo ke ho?",
     "What is this?"
    ],
    [
     "शौचालय **कहाँ** छ?",
     "śaucālaya kahā̃ cha?",
     "Where is the toilet?"
    ],
    [
     "यो **कति** पर्छ?",
     "yo kati parcha?",
     "How much does this cost?"
    ],
    [
     "बस **कहिले** आउँछ?",
     "bas kahile āũcha?",
     "When does the bus come?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Unlike English, the question word is **not moved to the front** — it stays in its natural place."
  }
 ],
 "7": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Politely ask someone to \"please ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: verb root + **नुहोस् (-nuhos)**"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Verb (meaning)",
    "Request form",
    "Romanized"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "आउनु (come)",
     "आउ**नुहोस्**",
     "āu**nuhos**"
    ],
    [
     "बस्नु (sit)",
     "बस्**नुहोस्**",
     "bas**nuhos**"
    ],
    [
     "सुन्नु (listen)",
     "सुन्**नुहोस्**",
     "sun**nuhos**"
    ],
    [
     "हेर्नु (look)",
     "हेर्**नुहोस्**",
     "her**nuhos**"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "ढोका **खोल्नुहोस्**।",
     "ḍhokā kholnuhos",
     "Please open the door"
    ],
    [
     "यहाँ नाम **लेख्नुहोस्**।",
     "yahā̃ nām lekhnuhos",
     "Please write your name here"
    ],
    [
     "**पर्खनुहोस्**।",
     "parkhanuhos",
     "Please wait"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Adding **नुहोस्** makes it polite — use it with elders and people you've just met."
  }
 ],
 "8": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Give commands at the right politeness level."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Three politeness levels"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Listener",
    "How to build",
    "Example (get up उठ्नु)",
    "Romanized",
    "Nuance"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "elder / polite",
     "root + **नुहोस्**",
     "उठ्**नुहोस्**",
     "uṭh**nuhos**",
     "please do ~"
    ],
    [
     "equal / mid",
     "root + **ऊ**",
     "उठ (≒उठ्**नू**)",
     "uṭh",
     "do ~"
    ],
    [
     "close / lower",
     "root only",
     "**उठ**",
     "uṭh",
     "do ~ (plain)"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning",
    "Level"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "यहाँ **आउनुहोस्**।",
     "yahā̃ āunuhos",
     "Come here",
     "polite"
    ],
    [
     "चाँडो **खाऊ**।",
     "cā̃ḍo khāū",
     "Eat quickly",
     "mid"
    ],
    [
     "ढोका बन्द **गर**।",
     "ḍhokā banda gar",
     "Close the door",
     "plain"
    ],
    [
     "चाँडो **उठ**।",
     "cā̃ḍo uṭh",
     "Wake up quickly",
     "plain"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "※ **कृपया (kripayā) = please**. Adding it softens the command (e.g., कृपया चुप लाग्नुहोस् = please be quiet)."
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Choose the level by your relationship. When in doubt, the polite **नुहोस्** is safe."
  }
 ],
 "9": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"you must not ~\" and \"please don't ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Two ways"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Way",
    "How to build",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "① rule / prohibition",
     "root + **नुहुँदैन** (-nuhũdaina)",
     "must not ~"
    ],
    [
     "② polite \"don't\"",
     "**न** + root + **नुहोस्**",
     "please don't ~"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning",
    "Type"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
