     "मैले हिउँ **देखेको छु**।",
     "maile hiũ dekheko chu",
     "I have seen snow"
    ],
    [
     "मैले हवाईजहाज **चढेको छु**।",
     "maile havāījahāj caḍheko chu",
     "I have ridden in an airplane"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "The form resembles the progressive (Theme 11, \"~इरहेको छु\"), but this is **एको छु (experience)** — no \"इ\". Don't forget **ले** on the subject."
  }
 ],
 "22": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"A is more ~ than B\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: **B + भन्दा (bhandā) + adjective** (more ~ than B)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Attach **भन्दा** to the thing you compare against."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "स्याउ **केराभन्दा** गुलियो छ।",
     "syāu kerābhandā guliyo cha",
     "Apples are sweeter than bananas"
    ],
    [
     "ऊ **मभन्दा** अग्लो छ।",
     "ū mabhandā aglo cha",
     "He is taller than me"
    ],
    [
     "आज **हिजोभन्दा** चिसो छ।",
     "āja hijobhandā ciso cha",
     "Today is colder than yesterday"
    ],
    [
     "**बसभन्दा** रेल छिटो छ।",
     "basbhandā rel chiṭo cha",
     "The train is faster than the bus"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "The adjective does not change (no \"-er\" form). Just add \"the other thing + भन्दा\"."
  }
 ],
 "23": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Connect words and sentences."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Common conjunctions"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Conjunction",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "र",
     "ra",
     "and (list)"
    ],
    [
     "तर",
     "tara",
     "but"
    ],
    [
     "~(भए)कोले",
     "(bhae)kole",
     "because / so"
    ],
    [
     "पनि…पनि",
     "pani…pani",
     "both … and"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "मलाई चिया **र** कफी मन पर्छ।",
     "malāī ciyā ra kaphī man parcha",
     "I like tea and coffee"
    ],
    [
     "ऊ विद्यार्थी हो **तर** काम गर्छ।",
     "ū vidyārthī ho tara kām garcha",
     "He is a student but works"
    ],
    [
     "थकित **भएकोले**, मैले चाँडो सुतेँ।",
     "thakit bhaekole, maile cā̃ḍo sutẽ",
     "Since I was tired, I slept early"
    ],
    [
     "उनी गाउन **पनि** नाच्न **पनि** राम्री छिन्।",
     "unī gāuna pani nācna pani rāmrī chin",
     "She is good at both singing and dancing"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "\"because\" = **कोले／भएकोले** at the end of the reason clause. \"both … and\" = **पनि** twice."
  }
 ],
 "24": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"~ while doing …\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: verb 1 root + **दै (-dai)** + verb 2"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "संगीत **सुन्दै** पढ्छु।",
     "saṅgīt sundai paḍhchu",
     "I study while listening to music"
    ],
    [
     "**हिँड्दै** कुरा गरौँ।",
     "hĩḍdai kurā garaũ",
     "Let's talk while walking"
    ],
    [
     "टेलिभिजन **हेर्दै** खाना खान्छु।",
     "ṭelibhijan herdai khānā khānchu",
     "I eat while watching television"
    ],
    [
     "कफी **पिउँदै** अखबार पढ्छु।",
     "kaphī piũdai akhbār paḍhchu",
     "I read the newspaper while drinking coffee"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Add **दै** to the \"while\" verb, and put the **main action last**."
  }
 ],
 "25": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"after doing ~, …\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: verb 1 root + **एपछि (-epachi)** + verb 2"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "हात **धोएपछि**, खान्छु।",
     "hāt dhoepachi, khānchu",
     "After washing my hands, I eat"
    ],
    [
     "**उठेपछि**, अनुहार धुन्छु।",
     "uṭhepachi, anuhār dhuncha",
     "After getting up, I wash my face"
    ],
    [
     "कफी **पिएपछि**, काम सुरु गर्छु।",
     "kaphī piepachi, kām suru garchu",
     "After drinking coffee, I start work"
    ],
    [
     "काठमाडौँ **आएपछि**, अङ्ग्रेजी पढ्न थालेँ।",
     "kāṭhmāḍaũ āepachi, aṅgrejī paḍhna thālẽ",
     "After coming to Kathmandu, I started studying English"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Theme 24 \"while (दै)\" is simultaneous; this \"after (एपछि)\" is sequence. The ending changes the meaning."
  }
 ],
 "26": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"in order to ~\" and \"for ~\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Two patterns"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Pattern",
    "Formula",
    "Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "① verb",
     "root + **नको लागि** (-nako lāgi)",
     "पढ्नको लागि (in order to study)"
    ],
    [
     "② noun",
     "noun + **को लागि** (ko lāgi)",
     "स्वास्थ्यको लागि (for health)"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "2. Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "**पढ्नको लागि**, पुस्तकालय जान्छु।",
     "paḍhnako lāgi, pustakālaya jānchu",
     "To study, I go to the library"
    ],
    [
     "**स्वास्थ्यको लागि**, हरेक दिन व्यायाम गर्छु।",
     "svāsthyako lāgi, harek din vyāyām garchu",
     "For my health, I exercise every day"
    ],
    [
     "साथीलाई **भेट्नको लागि**, स्टेशनसम्म गएँ।",
     "sāthīlāī bheṭnako lāgi, sṭeśansamma gaẽ",
     "To meet my friend, I went to the station"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "Verbs take **नको लागि**, nouns take **को लागि**. Put the purpose part first."
  }
 ],
 "27": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"if ~, then …\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: **यदि (yadi) ~ भने (bhane)**, …"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Start with यदि (if), and put **भने** (then/if) after the condition."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "**यदि** पानी पर्यो **भने**, छाता लिएर जान्छु।",
     "yadi pānī paryo bhane, chātā lier jānchu",
     "If it rains, I'll take an umbrella"
    ],
    [
     "**यदि** फुर्सद छ **भने**, आउनुस्।",
     "yadi phursad cha bhane, āunus",
     "If you're free, please come"
    ],
    [
     "**यदि** सस्तो छ **भने**, किन्छु।",
     "yadi sasto cha bhane, kinchu",
     "If it's cheap, I'll buy it"
    ],
    [
     "**यदि** उ आउँछ **भने**, म पनि जान्छु।",
     "yadi u āũcha bhane, ma pani jānchu",
     "If he comes, I'll go too"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "text": "**यदि** can be dropped, but keep **भने**. \"condition + भने\" = \"if ~\"."
  }
 ],
 "28": [
  {
   "type": "goal",
   "text": "Say \"~ is/was done\"."
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "1. Formula: root + **इयो (-iyo)** (was ~ed)"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Sentence",
    "Romanized",
    "Meaning"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "ढोका **खोलियो**।",
     "ḍhokā kholiyo",
     "The door was opened"
